index.js:
    It all start with index.js where we will first implement torrent parser to parse the file and 
    read the content there. 
    The Torrent Parser is implemented in src/torrent-parser which is entry point after index.js
    In the same file, after reading the file, we have the list of peers from tracker and start downloading
    it using src/download.

torrent-parser.js:
    First we import "graceful-fs" rather than "fs" because it provide an API similar to "fs", 
    but adds handling intended to make filesystem operation more resilient i.e. can easily 
    work with multiple file at once by queuing the file and handling information.
    Bancode is imported here because torrent are encoded in bencode format which are like 
    d3:cow3:mooe => {"cow":"moe"} or li3e4:spame => [3, "spam"] or i3e => 3 or 4:spam => "spam".
    Then crypto is imported because BitTorrent uses SHA-1 hashes for identifying/verifying pieces.
    Then bignum is imported to handle large integers that may be larger than safe range but in 
    torrent sizes, we would not need that big number but here we uses bignum to represent
    sizes as integer buffers.
    Then we have read the file which returns a raw byte of a torrent file as a Buffer.
    And then bencode.decode is used to get the bencode content. Here result is javascript object.

    So open returns torrent = {
        announce: ..,
        info: {
            name: ..,
            length: ..,
            "piece length": ..,
            pieces: ...
        }
    }
    // Here note that the pieces field contains SHA-1 hash of each piece present to verify that the 
    recieved piece is correct or not.


    Here Size takes the torrent file and calculates the total size. The torrent file is a metadata.
    torrent.info describes the actual content being downloaded.
    In this size checkes torrent.info.files becuase if files is there then it is a multi file torrent,
    otherwise it is a single file download.
    So if it is a single file then the file length is in the torrent.info.length and if it is a multi
    file then there is a list in files with each having piece length and the path.